    "text": "<p>Two masses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> are fixed together by a massless spring, A force acts on the mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> as shown in figure. If the mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> starts moving away from mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> with acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, then the acceleration of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> will be :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f72d7ccf-b456-4057-a75d-32c15dc1ce74-image.png\" style=\"width: 235px; height: 39px;\" /></p>",
